			"65": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": true
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "LOCAL MIN \/ MAX\n\nThe Local Min and Local Max nodes will calculate the local extrema in a collection. This is different from the regular Min and Max node that calculate the global extrema. The node will output the extrema as a float and give you the index of where of where in the collection the extrema is positioned.  In the inspector you can switch between the first or last local extrema.\n\nIn the example below we first create a complex array by inserting arrays into one another. This array is doubled in sized and mirrored by using the Expand node with its wrapping set to ping pong. The finished array is used to change the Y position of each circle.\n\nThe array is sent to all the min\/max nodes. We've added regular Min\/Max to demonstrate the difference. The index of each desired extremum is sent into a Join and Write so that we can assign the correct colors to the correct circles.\n\nD. BLUE = Local Min (First)\nRED = Local Max (First)\nL. BLUE = Min\nYELLOW = Max\nGREEN = Local Max (Last)\nPINK = Local Min (Last)"
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 426.736602783203125,
					"width": 882.68218994140625,
					"x": -410.580902099609375,
